From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xiaoxing Hu <hi@xiaoxing.dev>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:33:19 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] build: export only the C API from the Linux library

The shared library exported every symbol of the libraries linked into it
statically: FreeType, HarfBuzz, fontconfig, libxml2, libpng, zlib, Dear
ImGui, libc++ and the rest, 12,935 symbols in all.  Loaded into a process
that has the system's copies of some of them already, as a GTK application
has, the library's own calls to those symbols bind to the host's copies:
in Emacs, 1,047 of them went to the system's libxml2, FreeType, libpng,
HarfBuzz, fontconfig, zlib and libstdc++, while the rest stayed inside,
two versions of each library mixed in one call path.

A version script keeps everything but the ghostty_ functions local, so
the library calls its own copies and exports its API alone.
---
 src/build/GhosttyLib.zig |  8 ++++++++
 src/build/libghostty.map | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/build/libghostty.map

diff --git a/src/build/GhosttyLib.zig b/src/build/GhosttyLib.zig
index e340b5921..f88b9054a 100644
--- a/src/build/GhosttyLib.zig
+++ b/src/build/GhosttyLib.zig
@@ -110,6 +110,14 @@ pub fn initShared(
     });
     _ = try deps.add(lib);
 
+    // Export the C API alone. Otherwise the libraries linked in statically
+    // export their symbols too, and in a host that has loaded the system's
+    // copies of them, such as a GTK application, the library's calls to its
+    // own copies bind to the host's instead, another version of each.
+    if (deps.config.target.result.os.tag == .linux) {
+        lib.version_script = b.path("src/build/libghostty.map");
+    }
+
     // On Windows with MSVC, building a DLL requires the full CRT library
     // chain. linkLibC() (called via deps.add) provides msvcrt.lib, but
     // that references symbols in vcruntime.lib and ucrt.lib. Zig's library
diff --git a/src/build/libghostty.map b/src/build/libghostty.map
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..d58a9cbd8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/build/libghostty.map
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+/* What the shared library exports on Linux: the C API of include/ghostty.h,
+ * whose functions all start with ghostty_.  Everything else stays inside the
+ * library, so that its own copies of FreeType, HarfBuzz, fontconfig, libxml2,
+ * libpng, zlib and the rest are the ones it calls, even in a process that has
+ * loaded the system's copies first, as a host such as a GTK application has. */
+{
+    global:
+        ghostty_*;
+    local:
+        *;
+};
